  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The diameter of the circle is perpendicular distance between the parallel lines (tangents) \\(3 x-4 y+4=0\\) and \\(3 x-4 y-\\frac{7}{2}=0\\) and so it is equal to\n\\(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9+16}}+\\frac{7 / 2}{\\sqrt{9+16}}=\\frac{3}{2}\\). Hence radius is \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
